---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import SubscriptionProjector from '../../components/SubscriptionProjector.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Subscription Revenue Projector" description="Project MRR and customer count month-by-month based on new signups and churn rate.">
  <SubscriptionProjector client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why churn compounds</h2>
  <p>Even a modest monthly churn rate compounds significantly over a year — 5% monthly churn means roughly 46% of a starting cohort is gone within 12 months if no new customers were added.</p>

  <h2>Common Churn Projection Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Underestimating how much churn compounds</strong> over a full year, focusing only on the seemingly small monthly percentage.</li>
    <li><strong>Projecting flat new signups</strong> without accounting for how growth or marketing changes might shift acquisition rate month to month.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Subscription Projector</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Projecting future MRR based on current growth and churn trends</li>
    <li>Understanding how much new customer acquisition is needed to offset churn</li>
    <li>Modeling different growth scenarios for planning purposes</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
